00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:36.110
The space between a
model in development

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:38.270
and a model in
production is just

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.880
filled with pitfalls that
will catch the unprepared

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.590
machine learning engineer.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:44.870
These chasms can be
crossed, and this session

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:46.460
helps outline what
to watch out for

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:49.910
and the steps to take
via four broad areas--

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:54.900
reproducibility, portability,
flexibility, and agility.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.350
The first challenge
is reproducibility.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:59.120
Training and prediction
data, they've

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:01.980
got to have the same
pre-processing applied to them.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:05.450
So use tools like Apache
Beam, TensorFlow Transform,

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:06.980
and the TensorFlow
feature columns

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.950
API to help ensure that
the same code executes

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:13.040
during both training
and prediction.

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:16.430
Copying data around can also
cause all sorts of issues

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:18.200
when it comes to
reproducibility,

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.600
so don't do it if
you don't have to.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:24.350
Use tools that will allow you
to join your data in place.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.470
With tools like BigQuery,
Cloud Storage, Bigtable,

00:01:27.470 --> 00:01:31.280
and Google Sheets you can
perform operations in place

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.100
rather than making copies,
which can help eliminate

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.440
these reproducibility problems.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.687
Next up, portability.

00:01:38.687 --> 00:01:40.520
Models are trained in
different environments

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.020
from where they're deployed.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.270
Training is then
typically done on a server

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.490
with GPUs or even TPUs.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:48.560
But then, when a
model is deployed,

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.830
it might be in the
browser via JavaScript,

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.870
on mobile, including
Android or iOS, or maybe

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:56.840
on embedded systems,
like Raspberry Pis.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:59.030
So familiarize
yourself with the tools

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:03.800
used to modify trained
models for deployment,

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:08.690
like TF Lite or the TensorFlow
Graph Transform tool.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.390
The third chasm is flexibility.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:14.090
This can be interpreted a
couple of different ways.

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:18.080
It can refer to the model type,
data source and structure,

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:22.730
iteration speed of development,
model stacking, model swapping,

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:26.300
and scaling inference
up and down with demand.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.460
These flexibility
patterns allow your system

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:32.570
to be resilient to
changing requirements.

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:36.110
The final fourth
chasm is agility.

00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:39.290
Fail fast by testing new
ideas on smaller subsets

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:40.250
of your data.

00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:41.870
Keep iterating on
your model designs

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:44.660
and update your model
as new data comes in.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:46.280
Make sure you
version your models

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:49.010
so you can perform things
like AB testing, rollbacks,

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.690
and gradual rollouts.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.960
And don't let the perfect
be the enemy of the good.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.840
By making it easy to try
lots of different approaches,

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.180
you can stay agile
as the world changes

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:01.610
around you and your model.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:04.070
Get your model deployed in
production successfully using

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:07.580
these four principles of
reproducibility, portability,

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:09.890
flexibility, and agility.

